"will change (old value to new value) and getting their confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. module: ow_ai
#: model:ow.ai.tool,description:ow_ai.tool_update_records
msgid ""
"Change the values of records that already exist. Always call get_fields "
"first, and search beforehand for the exact records you mean to change, so "
"the domain you pass here targets only those; a domain that would match every"
" record on the model (an empty domain, or an always-true condition such as "
"an id filter every record satisfies) is refused, on purpose. \"updates\" is "
"a list of {\"model_name\", \"domain\", \"changes\"} groups (max 50; usually "
"you only need one), each matching at most 200 records; each \"changes\" item"
" is {\"field\": technical field name, \"value\": the new value, "
"\"x2m_commands\": null or a JSON string for many2many/one2many fields only}."
" Use \"value\" for every field except many2many/one2many ones, where "
"\"x2m_commands\" must instead be a JSON string such as {\"link\": [ids to "
"add]}, {\"unlink\": [ids to remove]}, {\"set\": [ids that should be the only"
" ones linked]} or {\"clear\": true} (only existing records can be linked; "
"never invent an id). Write a short, plain-language explanation of the "
"change, and when a field being changed represents a status or stage, also "
"explain what changing it will do. This tool always shows the user a preview "
"of the old and new value of every affected record first and only writes to "
"the database once they confirm; do not tell the user something was updated "
"until you see the confirmed result."
msgstr ""

